cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WRRA-M 0.3, please cite this research note."
title: "WRRA-M 0.3: Source-Law Filter Selection"
type: article
authors:
  - family-names: Choi
    given-names: Wonsik
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0001-4263-9772"
    email: "janefather@gmail.com"
version: "0.3"
date-released: 2026-09-30
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1"
url: "https://github.com/Wonsik-Choi-janefather/wrra-m-0.1"
abstract: >-
  WRRA-M 0.3 defines a four-filter admissible class that preserves the
  sixteen-channel space and common color action of version 0.2. Source
  supplies two scalar compatibility tables and Law scores each filter by
  summing the entries selected by its left and right matchings. Two selection
  gaps give a necessary and sufficient criterion: the version 0.2 cross filter
  is the unique maximizer exactly when both gaps are positive. A constant-score
  replicator flow then converges to the target from every interior initial
  condition, with an explicit exponential bound. The selection survives
  entrywise score perturbations of size rho when the smaller gap exceeds
  four rho. The numerical compatibility values and their physical origin are
  not derived.
keywords:
  - WRRA
  - Wonsik Reality Renderer Architecture
  - meta-dimensional
  - Source and Law
  - cross-dimensional filter
  - filter selection
  - selection gap
  - replicator dynamics
  - convergence
  - perturbation stability
  - Pati-Salam
